IMPORT prelude

-- Attorney-General (Additional Functions) Act 2014 (Singapore) -- when the Attorney-General may act as counsel for a statutory board
-- in court: the definitions (s 2), judicial review and follow-on claims (s 3), other court proceedings (s 4), the fee (s 5), and the
-- Schedule of relevant statutory boards (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1/7/2026), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/AGAFA2014.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated is Act 17 of 2026 (Skills and Workforce Development Agency Act 2026, in force 1 July 2026), which
-- puts item 23 in the Schedule. THE ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS IN THE DEPOSIT IS ONE OUT OF STEP WITH THE BODY (it numbers "Short title"
-- as 2); this encoding follows the body: s 1 short title, s 2 interpretation, s 3 judicial review, s 4 other proceedings, s 5 fees,
-- s 6 amendment of the Schedule.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0158 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 3 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. It asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short and is entirely encoded. For an ordinary person its effect is this: if you sue one of the listed
-- statutory boards (HDB, the CPF Board, IRAS, LTA and others), the State's own lawyer may appear against you, and the Attorney-General's
-- choice to do so cannot be questioned under the Act.
-- Not encoded: s 1 (short title); the President's power to amend the Schedule by order (s 6) beyond the Schedule as it now stands;
-- the amount of any fee (the Act sets none); and what "conflicting interests", "public interest" and "public importance" mean, which
-- are left to the Attorney-General's opinion and are taken here as given facts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions as shown by the example rows. No pipeline,
-- no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Attorney-General (Additional Functions) Act 2014 -- representation`

§§ `2 -- statutory boards and relevant statutory boards`

-- s 2: "statutory board" means "a body corporate or unincorporate established by or under any public Act to perform or discharge a
-- public function". "relevant statutory board" means "any statutory board specified in the Schedule".
GIVEN `established by or under a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `performs or discharges a public function` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a statutory board` IF
    `established by or under a public Act` AND `performs or discharges a public function`

-- The Schedule, "Relevant statutory boards", as deposited: 1 ACRA, 2 BCA, 3 [Deleted by Act 14 of 2022 wef 01/08/2022], 4 CPF Board,
-- 5 CAAS, 5A Communicable Diseases Agency [Act 4 of 2025 wef 01/04/2025], 6 EMA, 6A Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore
-- [Act 14 of 2022 wef 01/08/2022], 7 HSA, 8 HDB, 9 IMDA, 10 IRAS, 11 IPOS, 12 LTA, 13 MPA, 14 MAS, 15 NEA, 16 National Heritage Board,
-- 17 National Parks Board, 18 Presidential Elections Committee, 19 Public Transport Council, 20 Public Utilities Board, 21 Singapore
-- Food Agency, 22 SLA, 23 Skills and Workforce Development Agency [Act 17 of 2026 wef 01/07/2026], 24 URA. Twenty-five bodies.
-- The deposit does not say what item 3 was. The bodies below the line are ones the Schedule does not name (chosen as examples by
-- the encoder; whether each is a "statutory board" in the s 2 sense is not decided here).
DECLARE Body IS ONE OF
    `the Accounting and Corporate Regulatory Authority`
    `the Building and Construction Authority`
    `the Central Provident Fund Board`
    `the Civil Aviation Authority of Singapore`
    `the Communicable Diseases Agency`
    `the Energy Market Authority of Singapore`
    `the Gambling Regulatory Authority of Singapore`
    `the Health Sciences Authority`
    `the Housing and Development Board`
    `the Info-communications Media Development Authority`
    `the Inland Revenue Authority of Singapore`
    `the Intellectual Property Office of Singapore`
    `the Land Transport Authority of Singapore`
    `the Maritime and Port Authority of Singapore`
    `the Monetary Authority of Singapore`
    `the National Environment Agency`
    `the National Heritage Board`
    `the National Parks Board`
    `the Presidential Elections Committee`
    `the Public Transport Council`
    `the Public Utilities Board`
    `the Singapore Food Agency`
    `the Singapore Land Authority`
    `the Skills and Workforce Development Agency`
    `the Urban Redevelopment Authority`
    `the Singapore Tourism Board`
    `JTC Corporation`
    `Enterprise Singapore`
    `a town council`

GIVEN `the body` IS A Body
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the body is a relevant statutory board` IF
    CONSIDER `the body`
    WHEN `the Singapore Tourism Board` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `JTC Corporation` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `Enterprise Singapore` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a town council` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2 -- administrative decisions and judicial review`

-- s 2: "administrative decision" means "a decision of an administrative character which is, is proposed to be, or is required to be,
-- made (whether or not in the exercise of a discretion and whether before, on or after 1 January 2015) under any public Act".
-- A decision under a private Act, or one not of an administrative character, is outside the definition.
GIVEN `of an administrative character` IS A BOOLEAN, `made, proposed or required under a public Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an administrative decision` IF
    `of an administrative character` AND `made, proposed or required under a public Act`

-- s 3(1)(b) opens follow-on proceedings only "if a Mandatory Order, Prohibiting Order, Quashing Order or declaration is made pursuant
-- to the judicial review". An injunction is a judicial review remedy under s 2 ("an application for a declaration or an injunction"),
-- but it is NOT in the s 3(1)(b) list.
DECLARE Remedy IS ONE OF
    `a Mandatory Order`
    `a Prohibiting Order`
    `a Quashing Order`
    `a declaration`
    `an injunction`
    `no remedy`

GIVEN `the remedy` IS A Remedy
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the remedy opens section 3(1)(b)` IF
    CONSIDER `the remedy`
    WHEN `an injunction` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `no remedy` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `3 and 4 -- when the Attorney-General may represent the board`

-- s 3(1): the Attorney-General may represent a relevant statutory board in (a) "a judicial review instituted by any person in respect
-- of an administrative decision or instrument of legislative character of the relevant statutory board"; and (b) "any proceedings in
-- court (however instituted) for a liquidated sum, damages, equitable relief or restitution" if one of the listed remedies is made
-- pursuant to the judicial review; IF (c) the board requests it, (d) the responsible Minister consents, (e) the Attorney-General is of
-- the opinion that the Government and the board "have no conflicting interests", and (f) the Attorney-General is of the opinion that
-- representation "is not contrary to the public interest".
-- s 4(1): in "other proceedings in court (however instituted) not mentioned in section 3(1)", the same (a)-(c), and (d) the
-- Attorney-General is of the opinion that "the proceedings concern a matter of public importance".
--
-- So the s 3 test is negative (not contrary to the public interest) and the s 4 test is positive (a matter of public importance). A
-- money claim that follows a judicial review in which only an injunction was granted is not "mentioned in section 3(1)", so it falls
-- to the stricter s 4 test.
DECLARE ProceedingKind IS ONE OF
    `a judicial review of the board's decision or instrument`
    `a claim for money, equitable relief or restitution`
    `any other court proceedings`

DECLARE Route IS ONE OF
    `section 3(1)(a)`
    `section 3(1)(b)`
    `section 4`
    `no route`

DECLARE Matter HAS
    `the board` IS A Body
    `the kind` IS A ProceedingKind
    `remedy made in the judicial review` IS A Remedy
    `the board requested representation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the responsible Minister consented` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no conflicting interests in the Attorney-General's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `not contrary to the public interest in the Attorney-General's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a matter of public importance in the Attorney-General's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A Route
DECIDE `the route` IS
    IF NOT `the body is a relevant statutory board` (`the matter`'s `the board`) THEN `no route`
    ELSE IF `the matter`'s `the kind` EQUALS `a judicial review of the board's decision or instrument` THEN `section 3(1)(a)`
        ELSE IF `the matter`'s `the kind` EQUALS `a claim for money, equitable relief or restitution`
                AND `the remedy opens section 3(1)(b)` (`the matter`'s `remedy made in the judicial review`) THEN `section 3(1)(b)`
            ELSE `section 4`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the common conditions are met` IF
        `the matter`'s `the board requested representation`
    AND `the matter`'s `the responsible Minister consented`
    AND `the matter`'s `no conflicting interests in the Attorney-General's opinion`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Attorney-General may represent the board` IF
    CONSIDER `the route` `the matter`
    WHEN `no route` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 4` THEN `the common conditions are met` `the matter`
                          AND `the matter`'s `a matter of public importance in the Attorney-General's opinion`
    OTHERWISE `the common conditions are met` `the matter`
              AND `the matter`'s `not contrary to the public interest in the Attorney-General's opinion`

-- ss 3(2), 4(2): "Any decision made by the Attorney-General to, or not to, represent a relevant statutory board pursuant to
-- subsection (1) is final and conclusive." The Act gives no route of challenge either way. (Whether a court would still review such a
-- decision is a question of general law that the Act does not answer; not modelled.)
GIVEN `decided to represent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act lets the decision be challenged` IF
    FALSE

§§ `5 -- the fee`

-- s 5: the Attorney-General "may require a relevant statutory board to pay a fee of such reasonable amount as the Attorney-General
-- determines for representing the relevant statutory board in any proceedings in court mentioned in section 3 or 4, and that fee is to
-- be a charge on the funds of that statutory board". No figure is set. The Act puts the fee on the board, not on the other party.
DECLARE Payer IS ONE OF
    `the funds of the statutory board`
    `the other party to the proceedings`
    `the Government`
    `nobody`

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter, `the Attorney-General represented the board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fee may be required` IF
        `the Attorney-General represented the board`
    AND NOT (`the route` `the matter` EQUALS `no route`)

GIVEN `the matter` IS A Matter, `the Attorney-General represented the board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Payer
DECIDE `the fee is charged on` IS
    IF `a fee may be required` `the matter` `the Attorney-General represented the board`
    THEN `the funds of the statutory board`
    ELSE `nobody`
